  "note": "Complete current principal Rosenborg castle exterior and separate northwest gatehouse:long red-brick/stone-banded copper-gabled block,paired NE square towers/central faceted stair dome,tall SW tower with staged open lanterns,scroll gables/dormers/end oriels,chimneys,closed exterior entry doors,gatehouse open arch and skewed native plan,short mapped gatehouse approach,east bridge/rails with original lion/plinth cues,and low perimeter segments. Water/gardens,interiors,future underground treasury and independent park/street buildings are excluded. No native vertical tags. Original picture-proportional reconstruction scaled to47.04m plan:main eave13.5m/ridge20.4m,paired tower walls22.5m/tips34.8m,central stair dome21.6m and great tower wall28.5m/tip49.2m. These are approximate envelopes,not surveyed as-built heights. Roof/lantern/window/statue/scroll/grade inventories remain original approximations. +X southeast toward the lion/bridge end,-X northwest toward the separate gatehouse;+Z southwest toward the single tall Great Tower,-Z northeast toward the paired square towers and central faceted stair dome;+Y up. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
